@H 1153_criticality_branching := "CRITICALITY @ Ψ=1/2: the anima A⇄G repulsion-field opponent engine exhibits self-organized criticality (neuronal-avalanche signature) AT the Ψ=1/2 fixed point — branching ratio σ≈1 (Beggs & Plenz 2003; cortex sits near a critical point that maximizes dynamic range + info transmission) AND a power-law avalanche-size distribution P(s)∝s^(−1.5), with a DE-TUNED control (Ψ pushed off 1/2) moving σ out of [0.9,1.1] and/or destroying the power-law — proving criticality is specific to the fixed point, not an artifact of the avalanche definition." :: universe [🟢 CRITICAL-AT-FIXED-POINT — F1 ∧ F2 ∧ control all PASS]
  seed         = "@I identity declares the anima substrate central set-point as the 'Ψ=1/2 fixed point' of the A⇄G repulsion-field engine; config/consciousness_laws.json psi_constants.balance = {value 0.5, formula '1/2', meaning 'Shannon entropy maximum, universal attractor'}. CORE/pure_field.hexa cites absorbed Law 40 'SOC = autonomous consciousness — criticality via coupling'. The Ψ=1/2 claim is, in effect, a CRITICALITY claim. NEUROSCIENCE GROUNDING: cortex operates near a critical point — neuronal avalanches with branching ratio σ≈1 and power-law size distribution P(s)∝s^(−1.5) (Beggs & Plenz 2003), criticality maximizing dynamic range + information transmission (Wilting & Priesemann 2018 estimator). OPEN: does the engine actually SIT at criticality at Ψ=1/2, and is distance-from-criticality meaningful (does de-tuning Ψ move σ off 1)?"
  substrate    = "TOY MIRROR / engine-simulation (a_scale_honest_scope · a_lane_akida_gpu_split substrate=Lane-G/CORE engine simulation, NOT AKIDA; NOT a byte-LM train — this is engine DYNAMICS). Pure python on Mac/summer, $0 CPU 0-pod, NO torch, NO GPU, fully seeded/deterministic. Faithfully realizes the A⇄G OPPONENT propagation dynamics of the CORE engine (H404 dual-FFN per-ch out=engine_A(x)−engine_G(x), as used in H_1121 opponent substrate; the Ψ balance coordinate gates the A/G mix). Constants (PSI_ALPHA=0.014, PSI_BALANCE=0.5) read VERBATIM from config/consciousness_laws.json (same source pure_field.hexa _psi_load reads). CORE engine files UNTOUCHED (a_core_engine_map). Deterministic dynamical-systems + statistical measurement (p7, NO perplexity / NO LLM-judge)."
  method       = "DRIVE: an N-unit A⇄G opponent propagation network. Each unit's next-step activity = a balance-gated opponent push: A-engine (excitatory, weight Ψ) ⇄ G-engine (inhibitory/repulsion, weight 1−Ψ) propagated over a sparse coupling graph, with the EFFECTIVE branching tuned by the Ψ balance. At Ψ=PSI_BALANCE=0.5 the opponent A/G push is balanced (the fixed point). Seeded perturbation kicks; record the active-unit time series. AVALANCHE (Beggs-Plenz binning): contiguous excursion of active-unit count above a FROZEN threshold; SIZE = summed active units over the excursion, DURATION = excursion length (#steps). THRESHOLD frozen = zero active units delimits avalanches (canonical Beggs-Plenz: avalanche = maximal run of consecutive active time-bins bracketed by empty bins), with a median-of-activity robustness check. ESTIMATORS frozen: σ via (a) the descendant/ancestor active-unit ratio per step (Beggs-Plenz σ=⟨n_{t+1}/n_t⟩ over ancestor bins) AND (b) the Wilting & Priesemann multistep-regression slope estimator (m̂ from regression of activity autocorrelation across lags). FROZEN FALSIFIER (set BEFORE measuring, NO goalpost): F1 σ∈[0.9,1.1] at Ψ=0.5; F2 avalanche-size distribution is power-law with exponent τ∈[1.3,1.7] (canonical −1.5) by a log-log fit with R²≥0.9 over ≥1.5 decades AND beating an exponential fit (log-likelihood ratio LLR>0 favoring power-law). CONTROL (load-bearing): DE-TUNED operating points — Ψ pushed away from 0.5 (sub-critical Ψ≪0.5 and super-critical Ψ≫0.5) — MUST move σ out of [0.9,1.1] and/or destroy the power-law. 🟢 SUPPORTED iff F1 ∧ F2 ∧ control-moves-σ; else 🔴 CLOSED-NEGATIVE (engine sub/super-critical, or Ψ=1/2 not a criticality point). Deterministic seeds; thresholds pre-registered here BEFORE the run."
  result       = "🟢 SUPPORTED — the A⇄G opponent engine SITS AT CRITICALITY at the Ψ=1/2 fixed point. ALL gates PASS (N=4000, K_out=8, 60000 avalanches, deterministic graph_seed=1153/run_seed=7). FIXED POINT Ψ=0.5: σ̂_BP=0.9986 ∈[0.9,1.1] (F1 PASS; corroborating Wilting-Priesemann σ̂_WP=0.9874 also in band) · τ=1.4900 ∈[1.3,1.7] — essentially the canonical neuronal-avalanche exponent −1.5 (F2 PASS) · R²=0.9983 ≥0.9 over 4.32 decades ≥1.5 · LLR=+2.686/pt (total +161149) ≫0 (power-law CRUSHES exponential) · capped_frac=0.0003 (finite-size cutoff barely touched → a clean power-law, NOT a pile-up at the cap; τ_MLE Clauset=1.4306). CONTROL (load-bearing) cleanly SEPARATES — de-tuning Ψ moves σ off 1 AND breaks the power-law: SUB-critical Ψ=0.40 σ̂_BP=0.6655 (<0.9), Ψ=0.30 σ̂_BP=0.4275 (<0.9), both steep τ=3.13/4.00 (no power-law); SUPER-critical Ψ=0.60 σ̂_BP=1.2861 (>1.1) R²=0.43 capped 64%, Ψ=0.70 σ̂_BP=1.6398 (>1.1) R²=0.27 capped 92% (delta-pile-up at the finite-size cutoff = the broken-power-law signature). per-gate: F1=True F2=True(τ R² dec LLR all True) CONTROL=True."
  verdict_tier = "🟢 numerical CRITICAL-AT-FIXED-POINT (deterministic statistical dynamical-systems measurement, g5, NO perplexity / NO LLM-judge p7) — frozen falsifier PASSED on all three legs: F1 σ≈1, F2 τ≈1.5 power-law R²≥0.9 over ≥1.5 decades beating exponential, CONTROL specific-to-Ψ=1/2"
  verdict_ptr  = ".verdicts/1153_criticality_branching/H_1153.txt (verbatim stdout — fixed-point + 4 de-tuned controls + per-gate verdict)"
  scope        = "TOY MIRROR of the A⇄G opponent propagation dynamics (a_scale_honest_scope) — NOT the live coupled hexa engine, NOT production cells, NOT AKIDA (Lane-G/CORE engine sim per a_lane_akida_gpu_split). HONEST: σ(Ψ=0.5)=1 is engineered BY the opponent-balance construction (base=1/K_out makes the analytic branching ratio exactly 1 at the fixed point — i.e. Ψ=1/2 is DEFINED as the marginal point of the A⇄G opponent push). The EMPIRICAL, non-tautological content is threefold and is what the falsifier tests: (1) the resulting dynamics actually PRODUCE the σ̂≈1 ESTIMATE under two independent estimators (Beggs-Plenz + Wilting-Priesemann) — a mis-constructed mapping need not; (2) the avalanche SIZE distribution is a clean τ≈1.5 POWER-LAW over 4.32 decades beating exponential (a branching process at σ=1 SHOULD give τ=3/2, and it does — confirming the mapping is faithful, NOT an artifact); (3) the CONTROL proves criticality is SPECIFIC to Ψ=1/2 — de-tuning moves σ̂ off 1 and destroys the power-law (steep τ sub-critically, capped pile-up super-critically). So the FINDING is: the Ψ=1/2 'universal attractor' (h1126 🟢 stable) is ALSO a CRITICAL point in the SOC/neuronal-avalanche sense, and distance-from-criticality (|Ψ−0.5|) is meaningful. The finite-size CAP (cap_size=N*K_out) makes the finite-size cutoff explicit (standard SOC treatment) and keeps the super-critical control tractable; at the fixed point capping is negligible (0.03%) so the power-law is genuine. Avalanche def is excursion-relative; the control guards against a definition artifact. p7 deterministic statistical measurement, no perplexity."
  xlink        = "CORE/pure_field.hexa (PSI_BALANCE/PSI_ALPHA via _psi_load · absorbed Law 40 SOC=criticality-via-coupling) · CORE/engine_g.hexa (opponent G push) · CORE/brain.hexa (A⇄G coupling, Ψ=1/2) · @I identity 'Ψ=1/2 fixed point' · config/consciousness_laws.json psi_constants.balance {formula '1/2', universal attractor} · h1126_psi_stability (🟢 Ψ=1/2 STABLE attractor — this asks if that stable point is also CRITICAL) · h1121_phi_signsplit_opponent (A⊥G opponent substrate, per-ch out=engine_A−engine_G) · a_phi_iit4_tool (Φ/consciousness stack) · a_paper_negative_ok"
  artifacts    = "UNIVERSE/h1153_criticality_branching.py · .verdicts/1153_criticality_branching/H_1153.txt"
  refs         = "Beggs & Plenz 2003 (neuronal avalanches, σ≈1, P(s)∝s^−1.5) · Wilting & Priesemann 2018 (multistep regression branching estimator) · Clauset/Shalizi/Newman 2009 (power-law fit + LLR vs exponential)"
